      "id": 15695,
      "name": "Nepycros",
      "username": "Nepycros",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/n/8491ac/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2016-09-22T02:34:14.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>So, I think one of the greatest features of a digital adaptation for a card game is the removal of physical limitations. Namely, those involving Tokens of an Unlucky sort. They allow for some really ridiculous experiences.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Namely, the 1,000 Years of Bad Luck combo. You might be wondering, \"Who on earth is insane enough to accumulate 1,000 Unlucky Tokens in a single game session?\"</p><p>![](upload://4auDzQoaySNoMmzYieXbmiiBGNl.jpeg)</p><p>Could not tell you off the top of my head.</p><p>![](upload://rpNYXQbsN8HvRtdpSRr9V8LFeCK.png)</p><p>The good news is, we know the unlock conditions for Dark Watch Setback aren't related to having 1,000 tokens in the pool.</p><p>The better news is, with 2 High-Risk Behaviors out, anything you touch is vaporized.</p><p><span alt=\"\" class=\"broken-image\" title=\"This image is broken\"><svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-unlink svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use xlink:href=\"#unlink\"></use></svg></span></p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-13T15:26:21.553Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
