      "created_at": "2016-09-22T03:52:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Alternatively, I think that Dual Crowbars, Friendly Fire, and Fixed Point make a repeatable loop, limited only by the number of times you’re willing to click \"yes, I want to shoot Setback in the face \"</p>\n<p>Edit:</p>\n<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Powerhound_2000\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/powerhound_2000/48/1859_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Powerhound_2000:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>You think 1000 is high someone on Steam went even further <a href=\"http://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=767719887\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">http://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=767719887</a></p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>do you have any idea how that was achieved? That’s an average of over 4000 tokens per second since Setback was released last Friday.</p>",
